  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evidence-Based Humanitarian Response to People Affected by Earthquake in Kahramanmaras and Hatay Provinces of T&#xfc;rkiye</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The earthquakes that hit T&#xfc;rkiye on 6 February, resulted in more than 50,000 losses of human lives, affected 9 million people, and an estimated 3.3 million people displaced. Multi-sector needs assessments reveal that displaced population living in informal settings and in remote areas face food insecurity; lack of access to water, sanitation, education and livelihoods; lack of health assistance; are at risk of pandemic outbreaks, insecurity and environmental hazards. 
 
This six-month action is designed to provide evidence-based and integrated protection and water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH) interventions in Kahramanmaras and Hatay provinces. In coordination with the governmental authorities, humanitarian partners, and Temporary Settlement Support (TSS) sector, IOM, through its Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) is assessing the needs and vulnerabilities of nearly 1,200,000 internally displaced persons living in informal settlements, in 1,298 neighbourhoods of Kahramanmaras and Hatay provinces for referrals to humanitarian partners, including IOM programmes for service provision. Based on the findings of the assessment, the action contributes to the provision of safe and clean water, improved sanitation facilities including mobile laundry services, WASH non-food items, as well as enhance the health and well-being of affected populations in informal sites through hygiene promotion activities and integrated protection programming.</narrative>
  </description>
